{title: 624 - I Want Jesus to Walk With Me}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #624 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 624}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]I want Jesus [Gm]to [Dm/A]walk [Am]with [Dm]me.
[C7]I want [F]Jesus to [Dm]walk with me.
[Am]All along [Dm]my [Gm]pilgrim [C7]journey,
[Gm]I want Jesus [Dm/A]to [Gm]walk [Dm/A]with [Am]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]In my trials Lord, [Gm]walk [Dm/A]with [Am]me.
[C7]In my [F]trials [C7/G]Lord, [Dm]walk with me.
[Am]When the [Dm]shades [Gm]of life [C7]are [Dm]falling,
[Gm]I want Jesus [Dm/A]to [Gm]walk [Dm/A]with [Am]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm]In my sorrows, [Gm]Lord, [Dm/A]walk [Am]with [Dm]me.
[C7]In my [F]sorrows, Lord, [Dm]walk with me.
[Am]When my [Dm]heart within [Gm]is [C7]aching,
[Gm]I want Jesus [Dm/A]to [Gm]walk [Dm/A]with [Am]me.
{end_of_verse}
